==Trivia==
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [[Wikipedia:Duende|duendes]], [[Wikipedia:Kobold|kobolds]], [[Wikipedia:Leprechaun|leprechauns]], and [[Wikipedia:Ghoul|ghouls]].
**In the German and Dutch language settings of the game, the Goblin Cage's name translates to "Kobold Cage". In the Spanish, Italian, Russian, Arabic, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Goblin Cage's name translates to "Strongman's Cage", "Cage for Goblins", "Cage with Goblin", "Ghoul Cage", and "Leprechaun Cage" respectively.
***In the Japanese language setting of the game, The Goblin Brawler's name translates to "Revenge Goblin".
**The Goblin Cage is 1 of 17 [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblin Gang]], [[Baby Goblins]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Goblin Demolisher]], [[Suspicious Bush]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Goblin Curse]], [[Goblin Drill]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Party Rocket]], [[Party Hut]], [[Goblinstein]], and of course, Goblins.
***The Goblins, Spear Goblins, Goblin Cage and Goblin Hut are the only cards associated with Goblins that are unlocked in Goblin Stadium.
*The Goblin Brawler is inspired by a goblin prisoner character in the Clash-A-Rama episode "[[w:c:clasharama:%22Giant_vs._Giant_Problem%22|Giant vs. Giant Problem]]".
**In Clash Royale, the Goblin Brawler was imprisoned by the Goblins due to being too violent, as seen in a [https://www.youtube.com/shorts/A5iYQSUkBrI short].
*The Goblin Cage is one of the first [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] [[cards]] to receive a card render, alongside the [[Mortar]], [[Tesla]], and Goblin Hut.
*The Goblin Cage is one of the first cards to be featured in the [[Season Shop]], alongside the Goblins and Goblin Giant.
*The Goblin Brawler is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that has had its movement speed classification changed, the others being [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Elite Barbarians]], Suspicious Bush, [[Cannon Cart]], [[Lumberjack]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
*The Goblin Brawler resembles the [[w:c:clashofclans.fandom.com:Sneaky Goblin|Sneaky Goblin]] from Clash of Clans, although he has different clothing on.
*Its [[Star Points|Star Level 3 Skin]] grants the Goblin Brawler a red mohawk similar to the Level 6 Goblin in Clash of Clans.
*A broken Goblin Cage can be seen on the [[Trophies|Trophy Road]] as a decoration.
*The tattoo on Goblin Brawler's back appears to be a Healer, a troop from Clash of Clans.
*The Goblin Cage has been featured with multiple [[Buff|buffs]]. More specifically:
**The Goblin Cage is 1 of 2 buildings that has been featured with a [[Buff#Shield Boost|Shield Boost]] buff, the other being Goblin Hut.
**The Goblin Cage is the only building that has been featured with a [[Buff#Death Spawn|Death Spawn]] buff.
*The Goblin Brawler, along with the [[Minions]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], Dart Goblin, [[Elixir Golem]], [[Guards]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Executioner]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Royal Ghost]], and [[Lava Hound]], are featured as a [[w:c:squad-busters:Monsters|monster]] in [[w:c:squad-busters.fandom.com:Squad Busters|Squad Busters]].
**In Squad Busters, he is called "Uncaged Goblin", but in Clash Royale, he is called "Goblin Brawler".
*[[Chests|Gold Crates]] have an appearance similar to the Goblin Cage.
*The Goblin Cage is unavailable in [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|The Floor is Healing Challenge]], much like other building cards, as well as the [[Cannon Cart]].
*The Goblin Cage and the Goblin Brawler are the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
*In the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5_D51_eCAWg Season 3 reveal video], the text on screen incorrectly lists the Goblin Brawler's speed decrease as a range decrease.
*The Goblin Cage was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
